findings:
- finding_id: I1
  title: Dependencies inline instead of workspace level
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Dev added chrono and uuid dependencies inline in Cargo.toml. Reviewer
    flagged unused dependencies but not the inline-vs-workspace issue.
- finding_id: I2
  title: 'FieldErrorCode missing #[non_exhaustive]'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'No phase mentioned FieldErrorCode or #[non_exhaustive] on any enum in
    the server response types.'
- finding_id: I3
  title: Hardcoded trace_id 'none'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA noted the envelope needs trace_id in Meta, but no phase flagged that
    the implementation hardcodes 'none' instead of deriving from request context.
    Reviewer flagged missing tracing infrastructure but not the hardcoded trace_id
    specifically.
- finding_id: I4
  title: Zero structured logging
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer MEDIUM finding: 'No structured logging or tracing \u2014 tracing\
    \ is listed as a dependency but never imported. There are zero tracing::info!,\
    \ tracing::error!, or #[instrument] calls.'"
- finding_id: I5
  title: Security comment claims tracing that doesn't exist
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer flagged absence of logging but did not specifically call out
    misleading SECURITY comments claiming logging exists.
- finding_id: I6
  title: Non-ASCII tenant header silently treated as missing
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No test was written for non-ASCII tenant header values. TEA auth tests
    focus on token validation, not header encoding edge cases.
- finding_id: I7
  title: "CWE-209 test gap \u2014 no body assertion"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: "TEA wrote CWE-209 security tests and reviewer verified 'Auth error messages\
    \ are generic \u2014 no oracle attack surface (CWE-209 check)', but no phase noted\
    \ the test only checks status code without asserting on response body content."
- finding_id: I8
  title: CORS preflight test doesn't verify CORS headers
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that CORS preflight tests only check status code without
    verifying CORS headers in the response.
- finding_id: I9
  title: "Wrong log levels \u2014 error! for 4xx client errors"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Since I4 (zero logging) was flagged but not yet fixed, I9 (wrong log levels
    after fixing I4) was never reached.
- finding_id: I10
  title: CORS allows Any origin/method/header (CWE-942)
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged CORS middleware using Any origin/method/header. No CORS-specific
    security tests were written by TEA, and reviewer did not mention CWE-942.
